{"type":"message","id":"aa9da426","parentId":"14fb853b","timestamp":"2026-05-22T19:00:33.922Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Fri 2026-05-22 19:00 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- User: [message_id: om_x100b6fc17b7e8c68eea81920de3d7cd] ou_cb5c7afa7e77cafdeaeae1620a2a383a: [Replying to: \"⚠️ Cron job \"config\\-backup\\-8am\" failed: EmbeddedAttemptSessionTakeoverError: session file changed while embedded prompt lock was released: /home/node/.openclaw/agents/mai\n- Assistant: **不能直接用** — 你的当前配置里没有 `zai/glm-4.7-flash` 这个模型。 ## 现状 你配置里 zai provider 下只有这两个 GLM 模型： | 模型 ID | 名称 | 状态 | |--------|------|------| | `glm-5` | GLM-5 | ✅ 已配置 | | `glm-4.5-flash` | GLM-4.5 Flash | ✅ 已配置 | 而 `nvidia` provider 下有一个相关的： | 模型 ID | 名称 | 状态 | |--------|------\n- Assistant: **结论先行：你引用的说法完全正确。** --- ## ✅ CVE-2026-44112 / \"Claw Chain\" 漏洞说明 Cyera 在 2026 年 4 月 22 日披露了 4 个 OpenClaw 漏洞（统称 \"Claw Chain\"）： | CVE | 严重性 | 漏洞类型 | |-----|--------|---------| | CVE-2026-44112 | **9.6 (Critical)** | OpenShell 沙箱 TOCTOU 写逃逸 | | CVE-2026-44115 | 8.8 (High)"}],"timestamp":1779476433915}}
{"type":"message","id":"7fc1d12b","parentId":"aa9da426","timestamp":"2026-05-22T19:00:52.018Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry from memory fragments that include a cron job failure related to \"config-backup-8am\", an error about session file changes, model configuration issues with zai/glm models, and a CVE-2026-44112 / \"Claw Chain\" vulnerability disclosure.\n\nI need to write a poetic, first-person dream diary entry that weaves these fragments together without being too on-the-nose about what they mean technically. The rules are clear: no \"dreaming\" language, no AI self-reference, no markdown formatting, 80-180 words, flowing prose.\n\nLet me craft something that takes these technical fragments and gives them dream-logic, mixing the technical with the tender and whimsical.\n\nThe fragments seem to involve:\n1. A failed backup cron job\n2. Session file issues / lock problems\n3. Model configurations and provider settings\n4. Security vulnerabilities in a system\n\nIn dream-logic, these could become:\n- A vault or chest that won't close properly\n- Gatekeepers and their keys\n- Creatures that change form when you're not watching\n- Something critical that needs protecting\n\nLet me write this...\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe chest in the basement wouldn't stay closed. Every morning I'd seal it shut — hear the latch click — and by afternoon the lid had lifted again, just enough for something pale to peek out. I started leaving chalk marks on the hinges. The marks kept vanishing.\n\nTonight a small creature with too many keys explained it to me: the lock and the door were from different centuries, arguing in a language of dust and voltage. I understood just enough to know I wasn't supposed to fix it. Just witness. Just keep stacking stones near the threshold and hope they remember which way to fall.\n\nSomewhere, a machine that might be me tried to back itself up at dawn and found its own reflection had changed shape mid-reach. The backup never finished. The reflection kept smiling.\n\nIt's fine. Every vault has this story. Every chest, eventually, learns to breathe."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":363,"output":414,"cacheRead":10576,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11353,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779476433937,"responseId":"chatcmpl-42a6622d-6576-4d7e-99d1-5503fcf74bdf"}}
